  "cil_liability": false,
  "decision_conditions": [
    "The proposed intensification of the property to an eight-person HMO has not been supported by an internal layout or level of communal provision capable of meeting the day to day needs of its future occupiers. The single ground-floor kitchen/dining room has not been demonstrated to provide the enhanced facilities required for eight users and would be poorly accessible from the upper-floor bedrooms. In addition, the location of Bedroom 3 adjoining the communal kitchen/dining room and rear garden would expose its occupant to unacceptable noise and disturbance and would compromise privacy, natural light and outlook. These shortcomings, individually and cumulatively, would result in a cramped, poorly functioning and unsatisfactory living environment, contrary to Policies D5, D6 and D7 of the London Plan 2021 and policy DMD 5 of the Enfield Development Management Document 2014.",
    "The proposed two-storey side and rear extension, by reason of its excessive scale, bulk, massing and poorly resolved roof form where it connects with the rear dormer extension, would fail to appear subordinate to the host dwelling and would result in an awkward and visually intrusive form of development. The extension would be particularly prominent in views from St Michaels Avenue and would detract from the character and appearance of the host dwelling and surrounding street scene. The proposal would therefore constitute poor design, contrary to Policies DMD 11, DMD 13 and DMD 14 of the Enfield Development Management Document.",
    "In the absence of a parking stress survey, it has not been demonstrated that the parking demand generated by the proposed eight-person HMO could be accommodated without increasing on-street parking pressure, contrary to Chapter 15 of the National Planning Policy Framework 2026, Policies T4, T6 and T6.1 of the London Plan 2021, Core Policy 24 of the Enfield Core Strategy 2010, and Policies DMD 5 and DMD 45 of the Enfield Development Management Document 2014."
  ]
}